From 7141acf67b98d509af250e96074bc193974a68a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sahil Sagvekar <sahilsagvekar230@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 05:54:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Leave & Attendance: redesign for first-time users

- New layout: Today (check in, balances, apply) / My leave / Attendance /
  Team calendar / Approvals / Manage. HR screens moved under Manage.
- Apply for leave is a side panel (bottom sheet on phones): leave type
  cards with balance, Today/Tomorrow shortcuts, Full day / Morning /
  Afternoon, live summary (days, balance before -> after, who approves).
- Attendance: big check-in card, plain-word calendar with icons, 4 key
  numbers, tap a day -> "Fix this day" opens a prefilled correction.
- Approvals: one card per request with "also away" teammates, one-tap
  approve, reason required to reject, approve all, waiting-days badge.
- My requests show an approval timeline and full history; balance history
  in plain words.
- Team calendar becomes a day list on phones.
- HR Settings split into 5 sections; hours instead of minutes; plain
  labels with examples; leave types as expandable cards.
- Toasts for success, skeleton loaders, empty states, inline confirm
  instead of browser popups. Payroll screens keep their behaviour.

UI only: no API, database or rules changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
